<title>USA: MBIA qualifies nine municipal bond issues.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies nine municipal bond issues.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp. on Wednesday said it qualified the following nine municipal bond issues scheduled for competitive sale:</p>
<p>--Natomas Unified School District, Calif., $5.0 million Series A and $4.5 million Series B, both General Obligation (GOs) bonds.</p>
<p>--Bolyston, Mass, $2.8 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hastings, Mich., $3.3 million water and sewer is a direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Lincoln Charter Twp, Mich., $1.165 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Sturgis, Mich., $8 million electric revs is a direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Minnesota Higher Education, Minn., $24.440 million revenues.</p>
<p>--Farmington Municipal School District #5, N.M., $6.1 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Essex County, N.Y., $6.104 million GOs.</p>
<p>--North Tonawanda School District, N.Y., $3.386 million.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
